# One identity, three spellings. Without this the contributor graph splits a
# single author across three entries, which reads as a team that was never here.
#
# Canonical is the name and address the other public repositories use. The
# gmail address stays visible in the raw history of the earliest commits --
# a mailmap changes how git presents an author, not what was recorded.
foggylulu <fogelrobion.l@northeastern.edu> <lucafogelrobion@gmail.com>
foggylulu <fogelrobion.l@northeastern.edu> Luca Fogel Robion <fogelrobion.l@northeastern.edu>
